*     indirect_nul_prefix_name.sno -- ⛔ CHECKED IN RED ON PURPOSE (s194, row
*     `indirect-nonname-silent-accept`).  SPITBOL ACCEPTS a variable name whose
*     first byte is NUL -- &ALPHABET is 256 such bytes and $&ALPHABET is legal --
*     so this is NOT an ERROR 239 case and must never become one.  SCRIP's variable
*     namespace is C-string keyed (NV_GET_fn/NV_SET_fn take const char *), so a name
*     starting at a NUL cannot be spelled at all; SCRIP fails the statement instead,
*     which is what T1..T3 record.  &ERRTYPE stays 0 on those lines -- the refusal
*     costs no &ERRLIMIT credit, which is how this file proves it is a NAMESPACE
*     limitation and not a false 239.  It goes green when names become counted
*     strings; until then it is the pin on a limitation, not a regression.
        &ERRLIMIT = 100
        Z = &ALPHABET
        OUTPUT = 'SIZE(Z)=' SIZE(Z)
        A = $Z                          :F(F1)
        OUTPUT = 'T1 ok via var'        :(T2)
F1      OUTPUT = 'T1 ERR ' &ERRTYPE
T2      B = $&ALPHABET                  :F(F2)
        OUTPUT = 'T2 ok direct'         :(T3)
F2      OUTPUT = 'T2 ERR ' &ERRTYPE
T3      C = $(CHAR(0) 'X')              :F(F3)
        OUTPUT = 'T3 ok nulprefix'      :(T4)
F3      OUTPUT = 'T3 ERR ' &ERRTYPE
T4      D = $('X' CHAR(0) 'Y')          :F(F4)
        OUTPUT = 'T4 ok nulmid'         :(T5)
F4      OUTPUT = 'T4 ERR ' &ERRTYPE
T5      OUTPUT = 'END errlimit=' &ERRLIMIT
END
